cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SwiftCov, please cite it as below, and also cite bedtools, whose behaviour it reproduces."
title: "SwiftCov: a byte-identical drop-in replacement for bedtools coverage"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/joe-b-christensen/swiftcov"
authors:
  - family-names: Christensen
    given-names: Joe
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0908-1299"
    email: joechristensen@clin.au.dk
    affiliation: "Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit (TNU), Department of Clinical Medicine, Aarhus University, Denmark"
keywords:
  - bedtools
  - genome coverage
  - BED
  - performance
abstract: >-
  SwiftCov is bedtools v2.31.1 with a validated fast path for bedtools coverage on plain BED input; every other input
  runs the unmodified bedtools code. Its output is byte-identical to bedtools v2.31.1 on every input tested. On real
  HG002 reads with the query restricted to the chromosome that has reads, it was 13- to 34-fold faster than bedtools
  -sorted at one thread. With genome-wide queries, where most rows lie on chromosomes with no reads, it was 50-fold
  faster at two threads on 12.5 million chr21 alignments.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "BEDTools: a flexible suite of utilities for comparing genomic features"
    authors:
      - family-names: Quinlan
        given-names: Aaron R.
      - family-names: Hall
        given-names: Ira M.
    journal: Bioinformatics
    year: 2010
    volume: 26
    issue: 6
    start: 841
    end: 842
    doi: "10.1093/bioinformatics/btq033"
